for fans of horror movies halloween  isn't just one day in october  it's an axe wielding monster mashing  year-round state of mind  but you don't have to be david s  pumpkins to enjoy the spookier things in  life  how's it hanging all you have to do is  make sure you watch the very best horror  films that movie-making maniacs have to  offer  lucky for you 2018 has already provided  you with plenty of horror movies you  might have already missed  so hollow out that pumpkin and stick it  on your head here are a bunch of horror  movies from 2018 that you haven't seen  but probably should  we have such sites to show you  [Music]  annihilation beautiful awesome  restrained  and challenging annihilation is the best  film of 2018 that  odds are you haven't seen the movie  focuses on the aftermath of a meteor  strike that's given rise to an  inexplicable phenomenon with a wide area  of earth enveloped in an ever-expanding  shimmer  when five investigators enter to figure  out what's going on they find a  disorienting pocket world that's slowly  remixing itself in gorgeous disturbing  dangerous ways  it's a horror premise that creeps up on  you with the implication of the story  being nothing less than the doom of the  world  the second film from ex-machina director  alex garland it's a masterfully creepy  movie that deserves more attention than  it got in theaters  the endless indie filmmakers justin  benson and aaron scott morehead have  spent their careers putting together a  respectable catalog of genre-bending  films and the endless just might be  their best  casting themselves in the lead roles the  writer directors tell a story of two  brothers who flee a suicidal ufo cult  returning in adulthood to re-evaluate  the life they left behind  they discovered that there may indeed be  magic at the heart of the hippie  collective but if it's real  what does the otherworldly force  protecting the group want in return  made for very little money you only  notice the endless is low budget because  you're impressed by what they pull off  with beautiful cinematography and a  gorgeous california location  it's among the prettiest movies on this  list with a sense but not seen horror at  the heart of the story keeping things  tense through the whole run time  it's horror by way of hp lovecraft with  a story that sticks with you  low life it's not often that you get to  call a movie unhinged and really mean it  but lowlife  more than fits the bill a violent genre  bending almost farce that straddles the  border between horror  high comedy and human drama low life is  admirable for being both audaciously  plotted and technically slick  not cool calling me a nazi you don't  know my struggle  set in the scummy underbelly of los  angeles lowlife focuses on a number of  small-time criminals whose stories all  converge around an organ harvesting plot  gone wrong  it's a nightmare inspired by pulp  fiction but unlike most copycats this  one stands on its own  the end result is intense hilarious and  gross  despite feeling like it shouldn't work  at all low life is one of the year's  best and most savage  thrill rides marrowbone a quiet  self-assured mood piece of a horror  movie set in 1969  marrowbone introduces a mother and her  four children in the northeastern united  states  after the mother passes away the  children must maintain the illusion of a  healthy family in order to avoid being  made wards of the state  at the same time there's also a  supernatural threat within the walls  threatening to tear the family apart  from the inside out marrowbone received  middling reviews from critics having  some controversial late-game turns in  its plotting  but the twists in the story are  elegantly laid out even if you don't  like where the plot goes it's still a  well-designed movie accomplishing  everything it sets out to do with  patience and reserve  downrange on a road trip down an  isolated back road on a hot summer day  the tire of an suv explodes  as the young passengers set about making  repairs they're attacked by an unseen  sniper  who picks off a few victims leaving the  rest to huddle behind cover as they try  to figure out how to survive  like all good horror movies it's a  situation you can imagine yourself in  however outlandish it may seem  but downrange is more than just a good  concept it's good filmmaking with  quality gore effects giving every bullet  a real impact  it may devolve into campy territory by  the end but it stays entertaining all  the way through to watch the characters  struggle to puzzle their way out of  danger  if there even is any gonjium haunted  asylum  based on the local folklore surrounding  a real-life creepy location  gonjium haunted asylum is a korean  horror movie that wears its found  footage influences on its sleeve  easily among the scariest movies on the  list the concept of the movie is classic  forget complex mythologies gonjium is  about spending the night in a haunted  house  the movie follows a group of filmmakers  on a live horror webcast  trying to break a viewership record as  they broadcast live from a notorious  hospital  at first the program appears to be an  exercise in fakery  but the signs of a haunting become a lot  more convincing over the course of the  night  few horror movies capture a sense of  paralyzing dread like ganjium does  if you're looking for pure terrifying  white knuckle horror  it doesn't get much better than this  veronica  you should never believe hype that says  a movie is the scariest ever  in veronica's case it's not even the  scariest movie on this list  but this story of a young teen girl's  possession and slow corruption is a  well-crafted descent into madness  anchored by one strong character and her  otherworldly struggle with evil  veronica introduces the title character  as a caretaker for her younger siblings  mature capable and kind you can't help  but sympathize as something sinister  begins to wake up around her  she resists the evil defending her  siblings from harm like a true heroine  which makes the movie's bleak ending  such a gut punch the overblown hype for  veronica naturally led to a bit of  backlash  but take the movie on its own terms and  you'll get a well-done thought-provoking  possession narrative  not that scary but it's good
 

